Document structure: doctypes, head and body, content after the body,
misplaced html, head and body tags, frames, charset declarations, and
noscript.
-- Minimal --
-- in --
<title>T</title><p>Hello <b>world</b>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><title>T</title></head><body><p>Hello <b>world</b></p></body></html>
-- Empty --
-- in --
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body></body></html>
-- XHTML --
-- in --
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD XHTML 1.0 Strict//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/xhtml1/DTD/xhtml1-strict.dtd">
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xml:lang="en" lang="en">
<head>
<meta http-equiv="Content-Type" content="text/html; charset=utf-8"/>
<title>t</title>
</head>
<body><p>x<br/>y</p></body>
</html>

-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xml:lang="en" lang="en"><head>
<meta charset="UTF-8" />
<title>t</title>
</head>
<body><p>x<br />y</p>

</body></html>
-- Doctype --
-- in --
<!-- c --><!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.01//EN"><p>x
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- c -->
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><p>x</p></body></html>
-- XMLStylesheet --
-- in --
<?xml-stylesheet href="x.css"?><p>x</p>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<!--?xml-stylesheet href="x.css"?-->
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><p>x</p></body></html>
-- XMLDeclarationForms --
Only <?xml followed by whitespace or ?> is an XML declaration, as in
Universal mode: the other forms are processing instructions, which HTML
parsers read as bogus comments, like at the end of the input. The first
XML declaration before the root element is removed, and others are
written as comments like processing instructions.
-- in --
<?xml?foo bar><?xml><?xmlfoo?><?xml?a?><?xml	version="1.0"?><?xml?><p>a<?xml version="1.0"?>b<?xml
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<!--?xml?foo bar-->
<!--?xml-->
<!--?xmlfoo?-->
<!--?xml?a?-->
<!--?xml?-->
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><p>a<!--?xml version="1.0"?-->b<!--?xml--></p></body></html>
-- XMLDeclarationEmpty --
<?xml?> is an XML declaration.
-- in --
<?xml?><p>a
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><p>a</p></body></html>
-- XMLDeclarationTwice --
A second XML declaration is written as a comment, as HTML parsers read
it.
-- in --
<?xml version='1.0'?><?xml version='1.0'?><p>a
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<!--?xml version='1.0'?-->
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><p>a</p></body></html>
-- XMLDeclarationInBody --
An XML declaration after the start of the root element is written as a
comment, as HTML parsers read it.
-- in --
<!DOCTYPE html><p>a<?xml version="1.0"?>b
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><p>a<!--?xml version="1.0"?-->b</p></body></html>
-- CharsetMetaInexact --
HTML parsers match http-equiv values exactly (ASCII
case-insensitively), so the first two aren't charset declarations and
are kept. Declarations with an encoding label HTML parsers don't know,
or without one, are dropped too, so the output has one encoding
declaration.
-- in --
<meta http-equiv="Content-Type " content="text/html; charset=latin1"><meta http-equiv=" Content-Type"><meta HTTP-EQUIV=CONTENT-TYPE content="text/html;charset=latin1"><meta charset=latin1><meta http-equiv=content-type content=x><meta charset=x><meta Charset><meta http-equiv="Content-Type">
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><meta http-equiv="Content-Type " content="text/html; charset=latin1" /><meta http-equiv=" Content-Type" /></head><body></body></html>
-- CharsetMetaOtherAttributes --
Only the declaration is removed: the charset attribute, or http-equiv
with the content attribute it uses. A meta element with other attributes
(not counting xmlns, which is dropped from meta) is kept. HTML parsers use
the first of duplicate attributes, so the last one isn't a declaration.
-- in --
<meta charset=utf-8 name=viewport content="width=device-width"><meta http-equiv=content-type content="text/html; charset=x" id=a><meta charset=a http-equiv=Content-Type content=b name=c><meta charset=a xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><meta http-equiv=refresh http-equiv=content-type content=5><p><meta charset=x itemprop=y>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" /><meta id="a" /><meta name="c" /><meta http-equiv="refresh" content="5" /></head><body><p><meta itemprop="y" /></p></body></html>
-- CharsetMetaFirst1024 --
The charset meta element ends at byte 1024 of the output, where HTML
parsers still find it before parsing.
-- in --
<!----><p>a
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<!---->
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><p>a</p></body></html>
-- CharsetMetaPast1024 --
-- in --
<!----><p>a
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<!---->
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><p>a</p></body></html>
-- warn --
935: wrote the charset meta element past the first 1024 bytes (HTML parsers which aren't told the encoding will not find it before parsing the output)
-- CharsetMetaPast1024HTMLAttr --
-- in --
<html class=""><p>a
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html class="" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><p>a</p></body></html>
-- warn --
1115: wrote the charset meta element past the first 1024 bytes (HTML parsers which aren't told the encoding will not find it before parsing the output)
-- CharsetMetaPast1024HeadAttr --
-- in --
<head id=""><p>a
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head id=""><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><p>a</p></body></html>
-- warn --
0: wrote the charset meta element past the first 1024 bytes (HTML parsers which aren't told the encoding will not find it before parsing the output)
-- HeadContentAfterHead --
-- in --
<head><title>t</title></head><link rel=x><body>b
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><title>t</title><link rel="x" /></head><body>b</body></html>
-- SpaceAroundHead --
Whitespace before the head, which HTML parsers drop, is dropped, and
whitespace and comments after the head, which they put in the html element
while they put head content after them in the head, are written after the
head end tag.
-- in --
<html> <!-- a -->
<head><title>t</title></head>
<!-- b -->
<link rel=x>
<body>b
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><!-- a --><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><title>t</title><link rel="x" /></head>
<!-- b -->

<body>b</body></html>
-- CharsetMetaInPlace --
The charset meta element takes the place of a charset meta element first in
the head.
-- in --
<head>
  <meta charset=utf-8>
  <title>t</title>
</head>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <title>t</title>
</head><body></body></html>
-- CharsetMetaNotFirst --
-- in --
<head>
  <title>t</title>
  <meta http-equiv=content-type content="text/html; charset=utf-8">
</head>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <title>t</title>
  
</head><body></body></html>
-- SpaceAfterBodyInElement --
Whitespace after a body end tag which closed other elements is written in
them, as HTML parsers keep them open and put the whitespace in them. The
comment after it is written after the body end tag, where they put it.
-- in --
<body><div><p>x</body>
<!-- c -->
</html>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><div><p>x

</p></div></body><!-- c --></html>
-- CommentsAfterBody --
Comments after the body end tag are written after it, in the html element,
and comments after the html end tag after it, where HTML parsers put them.
The whitespace around them is written in the body.
-- in --
<body><p>x</p>
</body>
<!-- a -->
<!-- b -->
</html>
<!-- c -->
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><p>x</p>




</body><!-- a --><!-- b --></html><!-- c -->
-- CommentsAfterBodyContent --
A comment after content following a body end tag (d) is written in the
body, and one after an html end tag followed by a body end tag (f) after the
body end tag, where HTML parsers put them.
-- in --
<p>x</body> <!-- a --> <p>y</body><!-- b --></html> <!-- c --><div></div><!-- d --></body><!-- e --></html></body><!-- f -->
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><p>x  </p><p>y </p><div></div><!-- d --></body><!-- a --><!-- b --><!-- e --><!-- f --></html><!-- c -->
-- CommentsAfterIgnoredBodyEnd --
HTML parsers ignore a body end tag in a table cell or an object, and put
the comments after it in place.
-- in --
<table><tr><td>x</body><!-- a -->y</table><object></body><!-- b --></object></html><!-- c -->
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><table><tbody><tr><td>x<!-- a -->y</td></tr></tbody></table><object><!-- b --></object></body></html><!-- c -->
-- CommentsAfterHTMLEndClosingMisplacedHead --
An html end tag closing a misplaced head, which HTML parsers ignore, starts
the body, and the content after it is written after the html end tag or in
the body, where HTML parsers put it.
-- in --
<html></head><head></html> <!-- a -->x<!-- b -->
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body> x<!-- b --></body></html><!-- a -->
-- CommentsAfterBodyInForeign --
HTML parsers put a comment after a body or html end tag in the current
element when it is an SVG or MathML element.
-- in --
<body><svg><g></body> <!-- a --> </html><!-- b -->
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"><g> <!-- a --> <!-- b --></g></svg></body></html>
-- EndTagAfterBodyInForeign --
In SVG and MathML elements left open by a body end tag, HTML parsers apply
an end tag of one of them to it and the elements inside it, and keep the
insertion mode: the whitespace and comments after it go in the elements
still open, or the comments after the body end tag once only HTML elements
are open.
-- in --
<body><svg><g></body> </g> <!-- a --> </svg> <!-- b -->
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"><g> </g> <!-- a --> </svg> </body><!-- b --></html>
-- EndTagAfterBodyInForeignInP --
-- in quoted --
"<body><p><math><mrow></body></MROW>\x00<!-- a --></math> <!-- b -->"
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><p><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><mrow></mrow>�<!-- a --></math> </p></body><!-- b --></html>
-- warn --
35: replaced characters XML doesn't allow
-- ContentAfterBody --
-- in --
<body>x</body>y</html>z
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body>xyz</body></html>
-- NULAfterBodyInElement --
NUL after a body end tag which closed other elements is written in them
with the whitespace around it, and HTML parsers ignore it there.
-- in quoted --
"<body><p>x</body> \x00 "
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><p>x  </p></body></html>
-- NULAfterBodyInForeign --
In an SVG or MathML element left open by a body end tag, HTML parsers
replace NUL with U+FFFD.
-- in quoted --
"<body><svg><g></body> \x00 "
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"><g> � </g></svg></body></html>
-- warn --
22: replaced characters XML doesn't allow
-- EndTagAfterBodyInElement htmldiff --
-- in --
<body><a><div></body></a>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><a><div></div></a></body></html>
-- warn --
21: applied </a> after </body> closed div (HTML parsers would have kept div open when applying it)
-- ContentAfterBodyInForeign htmldiff --
-- in --
<body><svg></body>x
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"></svg>x</body></html>
-- warn --
18: wrote content after </body> outside the svg it closed (HTML parsers would have kept svg open and put the content in it)
-- IgnoredEndTagAfterBodyInElement --
-- in --
<body><a><div></body></b>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><a><div></div></a></body></html>
-- StrayEndTagAfterBodyInElement htmldiff --
-- in --
<html><a></html></p></br>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><a></a><p></p><br /></body></html>
-- warn --
16: wrote content after </html> outside the a it closed (HTML parsers would have kept a open and put the content in it)
-- ContentAfterBodyInElement htmldiff --
HTML parsers keep the a open after </html>
-- in --
<html><a></html>x
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><a></a>x</body></html>
-- warn --
16: wrote content after </html> outside the a it closed (HTML parsers would have kept a open and put the content in it)
-- ContentAfterMisplacedBodyEnd htmldiff --
the end tag of a misplaced body closes the a for the Reader
-- in --
x<body><a></body>y
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body>x<a></a>y</body></html>
-- warn --
17: wrote content after </body> outside the a it closed (HTML parsers would have kept a open and put the content in it)
-- ContentAfterBodyEndInElement htmldiff --
-- in --
<body><div>x</body><p>y
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><div>x</div><p>y</p></body></html>
-- warn --
19: wrote content after </body> outside the div it closed (HTML parsers would have kept div open and put the content in it)
-- MisplacedBody --
-- in --
<body class=a><p>x<body><html><head id=c>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body class="a"><p>x</p></body></html>
-- MisplacedBodyAttrs htmldiff --
-- in --
<body class=a><p>x<body id=b>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body class="a"><p>x</p></body></html>
-- warn --
18: dropped attributes of misplaced <body> (HTML parsers would have added them to the existing element)
-- Frame --
-- in --
<frame>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><frame /></body></html>
-- warn --
0: kept frame outside a frameset (HTML parsers would have ignored it)
-- FramesetInBody --
-- in --
<p>a<frameset>b</frameset>c</p>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><p>a<frameset>b</frameset>c</p></body></html>
-- warn --
4: wrote frameset in the body (frameset documents aren't supported, and HTML parsers would have ignored it after body content)
-- Noscript --
-- in --
<noscript><img src=a></noscript>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><noscript></noscript></head><body><img src="a" /></body></html>
-- HeadNoscript --
with scripting disabled, content other than link, meta, style, etc.
closes a noscript in the head
-- in --
<head><noscript><link rel=a><style>p{}</style></head></noscript><noscript> <meta name=x>x</noscript>y<noscript><p>z</noscript>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><noscript><link rel="a" /><style>p{}</style></noscript><noscript> <meta name="x" /></noscript></head><body>xy<noscript><p>z</p></noscript></body></html>
-- ImpliedHeadNoscript --
-- in --
<noscript><link rel=a><style>p{}</style></noscript><p>x<html><noscript><img src=a></noscript>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><noscript><link rel="a" /><style>p{}</style></noscript></head><body><p>x<noscript><img src="a" /></noscript></p></body></html>
-- ImpliedHeadNoscriptText htmldiff nonidempotent --
-- in --
<noscript>x</noscript>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><noscript>x</noscript></head><body></body></html>
-- warn --
10: kept text in a noscript in the implied head (HTML parsers would have closed the noscript and moved the text to the body)
-- ImpliedHeadNoscriptTitle htmldiff nonidempotent --
-- in --
<html><noscript><title>t</title></noscript><img src=a>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><noscript><title>t</title></noscript></head><body><img src="a" /></body></html>
-- warn --
16: kept title in a noscript in the implied head (HTML parsers would have closed the noscript before it)
-- ImpliedHeadNoscriptEndTag htmldiff --
-- in --
<noscript></html> x
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><noscript></noscript></head><body> x</body></html>
-- warn --
10: applied </html> in a noscript in the implied head (HTML parsers would have ignored it)
-- ImpliedHeadNoscriptClosedEndTag htmldiff --
the a starts the body, closing the noscript and the head; HTML
parsers ignore the noscript end tag, and keep the a open
-- in --
<noscript><a></noscript>x
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><noscript></noscript></head><body><a></a>x</body></html>
-- warn --
24: wrote content after </noscript> outside the a it closed (HTML parsers would have kept a open and put the content in it)
-- NoscriptAfterHead --
noscript after the head (also implied, or ended by a stray </head>)
is in the body
-- in --
</head><noscript>x</noscript><title>t</title></head><noscript><p>y</noscript>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><noscript>x</noscript><title>t</title><noscript><p>y</p></noscript></body></html>
-- MisplacedHeadNoscript htmldiff --
the head start tag after the body content is ignored by HTML
parsers, so the noscript is in the body
-- in --
0<head><noscript>x</noscript>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body>0<noscript></noscript>x</body></html>
-- warn --
17: closed noscript after a misplaced <head> at the content after it (HTML parsers would have kept it open as body content)
-- MisplacedHeadNoscriptHeadContent --
-- in --
<p>0</p><head><noscript><link rel=a></noscript>x
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><p>0</p><noscript><link rel="a" /></noscript>x</body></html>
-- BodyNoscriptEndTagClosesP htmldiff --
the noscript end tag is ignored when the p is open
-- in --
<body><noscript><p>x</noscript>y<noscript><div>z</noscript>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><noscript><p>x</p></noscript>y<noscript><div>z</div></noscript></body></html>
-- warn --
31: wrote content after </noscript> outside the p it closed (HTML parsers would have kept p open and put the content in it)
-- BodyNoscriptEndTag --
-- in --
<body><noscript><b>x</noscript>y
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /></head><body><noscript><b>x</b></noscript><b>y</b></body></html>
-- HeadNoscriptNested --
-- in --
<head><noscript><noscript class=a><!--c--></noscript>
-- out --
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><noscript><noscript class="a"><!--c--></noscript></noscript></head><body></body></html>
-- warn --
16: kept noscript inside a noscript in the head (HTML parsers would have ignored it)
